sdata> -- Issue #69: comma-line-continuation buffering is REPL-only logic (batch
sdata> -- mode reads the whole file at once, so a mid-file trailing comma is never
sdata> -- distinguished from any other character). "PRINT X Y," ends with a
sdata> -- trailing comma before a newline, so the lexer swallows the comma+newline
sdata> -- and the REPL keeps buffering (prompt switches to "..>") until "Z"
sdata> -- arrives on the next line, completing "PRINT X Y Z" as a single statement.
sdata> REPEAT 1
sdata> LET X = 1
sdata> LET Y = 2
sdata> LET Z = 3
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 1 records and 3 variables processed.
sdata> PRINT X Y,
..> Z
sdata> RUN
1.00000 2.00000 3.00000
RUN complete. 1 records and 3 variables processed.
sdata> QUIT
